Z||000000||pHoOl||09-28-2001||02:15 PM||||I decided the other day to check out my times.  mine is an 88GT with auto, and 127k miles.  I did two runs....<P>10.56---- with throttle position sensor not working<P>11.46---- tps working<P>Granted, these times were obtained with me running the stopwatch in the car.  But should the numbers even be that high?  What are some other GT times?<P>Thanks all!<P>------------------<BR>Rice mobiles are like tampons... Every p@#%y has one.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>        <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/phoolsig2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fformula88||09-28-2001||02:23 PM||||Those times sound awfully high.  With that kind of milage, maybe that engine is getting a little tired.<P>My best run timed was an 8.57 with auto my 88 Formula (also a stopwatch, but its still fairly accurate.)  I can consistently run between 8.7 and 8.9 sec to 60 mph.  The drivetrain is stock on the car.<P>Either your passing out from the high G-forces of a Fiero acceleration for 10 sec before awakening and pushing the button  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> j/k... or you've got a slow GT.||||reg||1
Z||000002||pHoOl||09-28-2001||02:39 PM||||This also reminds me... i checked 0-30.  i heard that fieros could pull 2.2     i got 4.4..<P>Any ideas on what might be slowing me down at 127K miles?  or would i end up having to rebuild to get it faster?<P>------------------<BR>Rice mobiles are like tampons... Every p@#%y has one.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>        <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/phoolsig2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Alex4mula||09-28-2001||04:55 PM||||My 117K miles stock auto 88 Formula does 8.5 too. Measured ona a G-Tech. I hear GTs are slower due to added weight but that is to much. Time for tune up.||||reg||1
Z||000004||pherder||09-28-2001||05:04 PM||||Do you have the cat. converter still?  Is it the original one?<P>If so, it might be plugged up enough to kill your acceleration.<P>I had an 87 GT w/auto that wouldn't get out of it's own way ... also it wouldn't shift very well so I took it to an tranny shop.<P>They told me to get the exhaust system checked out because the tranny was working okay as far as they could tell (road test).<P>This car had the factory stock cat. convertor on it still and when it was cut out (and replaced with a new, high flow version and about 1/2 the size!) I had a different car to drive!!<P>Now, if you don't have a cat. converter on the car ... never mind!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Paul<P>------------------<BR>Paul Herder<BR>88 Formula - Artero kit car doner and 350 TPI<BR>86 SE - 3.2 w/440T4 Transaxle<BR>95 GMC - 350 TBI - Factory "Custom"<BR>92 Mazda Protege - Stock<BR>55 Jones - First Edition WIFE- all mods, equipment,updates :D<BR>Sedgwick, KS 67135||||reg||5
Z||000005||Master_Sushi||09-28-2001||08:03 PM||||I've got 0-60 in under 10 secs with my 88 coupe auto. This is with an iron duck/duke/chef  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. Something can't be right if your at like 11 with the V6.<P>Also this might be a bit off topic. But does anyone know the 0-60 times for an 84SE 4.10 4 speed trans? My 84 seems WAY faster then my 88 and I was just curious.||||reg||1
Z||000006||pHoOl||09-29-2001||05:00 PM||||I believe that it is still the stock cat. on the car.  Is there any way to check if it is clogged without cutting it out and welding in a new one?  The other thing that my dad had mentioned was the air filter, which hasn't been changed since i got the car in february 2000.  (Guy said that he had just changed it).<P>I looked at the air filter, which didn't seem that dirty, but i think i'm gonna replace it with a drop in K&N to rule that out.  Any other ideas?<P>------------------<BR>Rice mobiles are like tampons... Every p@#%y has one.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>        <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/phoolsig2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||fiero56||09-29-2001||05:29 PM||||v-6 air filter gets dirty from inside-out. tune-up, air filter, fuel filter, plugs, wires, cap, rotor, etc.<P>MotorWeek got 9.5 out of a brand new '85GT auto, I don't think the '88GT would be much faster, if any.||||reg||1
